      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM** — All checks pass. [[trajectory](go/traj/40e62ad3-71a3-412b-a75a-e3aad9d94486)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** The fix is well-reasoned and correctly implemented. Pre-acquiring `crec_flash_lock_mapped_storage` before `unlock_rollback()` (which disables interrupts) ensures that if the mutex is contended, the thread will yield while interrupts are still enabled and the MPU is active, avoiding a kernel panic or unsafe thread suspension.\n*   **Security:** No security issues introduced. The MPU protection window remains appropriately small, and the mapped storage lock is properly released even if the read fails. \n*   **Style:** The changes are clean, easy to read, and consistent with the use of `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_EXTERNAL_STORAGE)` seen elsewhere in the file (e.g., in `rollback_update()`). The use of braces for single-line blocks also matches the existing file conventions.\n*   **Consistency:** The added locks mirror the logic found elsewhere for safely interacting with external storage. \n*   **Testing:** The test `zmake -D build helipilot --clobber` ensures it doesn\u0027t break the build for helipilot.\n\nGreat catch and solid fix!",
